/S /H2
/P 1419 0 R
/T (The rule of 3 is another design principle that states that if a class requires a user-defined destructor, a user-defined copy constructor, or a user-defined copy-assignment operator then it almost certainly requires all three.)
/E (The rule of 3 is another design principle that states that if a class requires a user-defined destructor, a user-defined copy constructor, or a user-defined copy-assignment operator then it almost certainly requires all three.)
/Pg 10 0 R
